---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Cta from "../components/Cta.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site.js";

const f = SITE.founder;
---

<Base
  title="About Kulvir Sharma, Founder | Kool Konsulting Nagpur"
  description="Kool Konsulting is run by Kulvir Sharma from Nagpur: finance and management training, M&A advisory background, and experience building a venture end to end."
  path="/about"
  ogSlug="about"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "About", href: "/about" }]}
  schema={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "@id": `${SITE.origin}/about#kulvir`,
      name: f.name,
      jobTitle: "Founder",
      worksFor: { "@id": `${SITE.origin}/#organisation` },
      address: {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        addressLocality: SITE.address.locality,
        addressRegion: SITE.address.region,
        addressCountry: SITE.address.country,
      },
      alumniOf: [
        { "@type": "CollegeOrUniversity", name: "The University of Melbourne" },
        { "@type": "CollegeOrUniversity", name: "University of Delhi" },
      ],
      knowsAbout: [
        "Local SEO",
        "Google Business Profile",
        "Financial modelling",
        "Business planning",
        "Workflow automation",
        "AI agents",
      ],
    },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label label-accent">About</p>
      <h1 class="t-hero" style="max-width:16ch;margin-top:1rem;">
        One person you can reach, accountable for the whole job.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="wrap founder">
      <div class="prose" style="max-width:62ch;">
        <p>
          Kool Konsulting is run by <strong>{f.name}</strong> from Nagpur. It exists
          because of a gap that is easy to see once you have worked on both sides of
          it: the firms that write the strategy do not build anything, and the
          agencies that build things were never shown the strategy.
        </p>
        <p>
          The owner ends up as the integration layer — briefing a consultant, then
          re-briefing a web agency, then a third supplier for automation, and
          personally carrying the context between all of them. Things get lost in
          those handovers, and it is usually the reason the plan never quite lands.
        </p>
        <p>
          Kulvir's training is in finance — a Bachelor of Commerce in Finance and
          Management from the University of Melbourne, with work in M&amp;A and
          corporate advisory where the discipline is that every number in a model
          traces back to a stated assumption. He has also built and run his own
          venture, which is where the other half comes from: knowing what it costs to
          actually ship the thing, not just to recommend it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those two halves are the firm. A market-entry study and the website the
          expansion needs are the same engagement here, done by the same person, so
          nothing has to survive a handover.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="panel">
        {f.photo ? (
          <img
            src={f.photo}
            alt={f.photoAlt}
            width={f.photoWidth}
            height={f.photoHeight}
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            class="panel__img"
          />
        ) : (
          /* No stock photography and no "coming soon" box. A typographic panel
             holds the space honestly until a real photograph is supplied. */
          <div class="panel__type">
            <p class="panel__name">{f.name}</p>
            <p class="panel__role">Founder · Nagpur</p>
          </div>
        )}
        <div class="panel__meta">
          <p class="panel__q">Direct line</p>
          <p><a href="/contact" class="link-u">Book a call with Kulvir</a></p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section invert">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Background</p>
      <h2 class="t-display" style="margin-top:0.9rem;max-width:20ch;">
        Training, and the work behind it.
      </h2>
      <ul class="creds">
        {f.credentials.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <span class="creds__t">{c.title}</span>
            <span class="creds__o">{c.org}</span>
            <span class="creds__m">{c.meta}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">How we work</p>
      <h2 class="t-display" style="margin-top:0.9rem;max-width:20ch;">
        Four commitments, and what each one costs us.
      </h2>

      <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);">
        <div class="val">
          <h3 class="t-sub">We publish our prices</h3>
          <p>
            Every service page states a starting figure. It costs us the enquiries
            from people for whom we are too expensive — which is the point. Neither
            of us should spend two meetings discovering that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="val">
          <h3 class="t-sub">We say when to buy something else</h3>
          <p>
            If Tally, Zoho or a template site genuinely covers your case, that is what
            we will tell you, and we will not invoice for the conversation. Building
            something you did not need is a bad first project and a worse reference.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="val">
          <h3 class="t-sub">You keep everything</h3>
          <p>
            Repositories in your name, models as working files, your Google profile
            registered to your own account. Making a client dependent is a business
            model. It is not this one.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="val">
          <h3 class="t-sub">We report the flat months too</h3>
          <p>
            Local visibility work has months where the numbers do not move. You will
            hear about those in the same report and in the same tone as the good ones,
            along with what we are changing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="notfor">
        <h2 class="label" style="margin:0 0 0.85rem;">Who we are not for</h2>
        <p>
          Businesses wanting the cheapest available option, anyone needing work
          started tomorrow, and large organisations that need a panel of specialists
          rather than one accountable person. A firm this size is an advantage in
          speed and access — it is not an advantage in headcount.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta heading="Work with Kulvir directly." />
</Base>

<style>
  .founder { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  @media (min-width: 940px) { .founder { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; align-items: start; } }

  .panel { border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--panel); }
  .panel__img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .panel__type {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .panel__name { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0; }
  .panel__role { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .panel__meta { padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); }
  .panel__q { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.875rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .panel__meta p { margin: 0; }

  .creds { list-style: none; margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .creds li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem 2rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(20, 19, 15, 0.22);
  }
  .creds li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(20, 19, 15, 0.22); }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .creds li { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.2fr 12rem; align-items: baseline; } }
  .creds__t { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.4rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .creds__o { color: rgba(20, 19, 15, 0.78); font-size: 0.9875rem; }
  .creds__m { font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgba(20, 19, 15, 0.6); }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .creds__m { text-align: right; } }

  .val { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1.25rem; }
  .val h3 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .val p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 0.9875rem; max-width: 48ch; }

  .notfor { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem; max-width: 60rem; }
  .notfor p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); max-width: 62ch; }
</style>
